Subject: [PATCH] vo_mediacodec: present a delayed OSD plane on every video frame

--vo-mediacodec-osd-vsync-delay=1 lines subtitles up with their picture on
Amlogic boxes, but there it made the video judder. On an S905X4 (SEI Box R
4K Plus, the chip of the Onn 4K Pro in Plezy #2894) at 4K59.94 with 23.976
content and dialogue subtitles, SurfaceFlinger showed 30 of 2,200 frames
held a refresh long and as many a refresh short, while the OSD plane was
presented 49 times, only when a subtitle changed. With a subtitle that
changed on every frame the same delay put in no judder.

A delayed plane is now presented on every video frame: vo_mediacodec sets
osd_ahead's repeat_unchanged (0214) together with the delay, so a frame
whose OSD did not change gets a result too, and the presenter draws the
slot on screen again from the composed canvas and swaps it at that frame's
delayed timestamp. At the default delay 0 nothing changes.

Measured with the delay at 1, on SurfaceFlinger and on HDMI captures of
clips that draw the frame index into the picture and into the subtitle
(one cue per frame, or 2 s cues with 1 s gaps):
- S905X4, 4K59.94: 1 judder pair in 2,196 frames (30 in 2,200 before).
  The subtitle is on its picture on all 1,308 captured refreshes of the
  per-frame clip and at all 55 cue edges of the sparse one.
- S905X4, 4K23.976: no judder before or after (2,216 and 2,191 frames);
  all cue edges in 2,395 captured refreshes on their frame.
- Google TV Streamer (MediaTek MT8696), 4K60 and 1080p23.976: the
  subtitle on its picture on every captured refresh of the per-frame clip
  and at every cue edge (52 at 4K60). The 4K60 cadence is the same as
  before.

While the delay is on, the plane costs a swap per video frame instead of
one per subtitle change. The render thread already rendered every frame to
find it unchanged; a repeat adds no upload, only a draw of the composed
canvas.

diff --git a/DOCS/man/vo.rst b/DOCS/man/vo.rst
index 1dca159..3d7d4c2 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/vo.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/vo.rst
@@ -795,7 +795,10 @@ Available video output drivers are:
     that many display periods after the video's timestamp. Some hardware
     codec paths put the picture on screen a vsync after a GL layer given the
     same timestamp; the embedder supplies the offset it measured. Only the
-    presentation time is shifted, the rendered pts is not.
+    presentation time is shifted, the rendered pts is not. A delayed plane
+    is presented on every video frame, its unchanged content again, rather
+    than only when the content changes; on Amlogic, updates that arrived
+    only with a subtitle change made the video judder.
 
     ``--vo-mediacodec-letterbox-fill=<yes|no>`` (default yes) fills the OSD
     plane outside the video rectangle opaque black. The OSD Surface spans
diff --git a/video/out/vo_mediacodec.c b/video/out/vo_mediacodec.c
index 318e06e..d5ac76c 100644
--- a/video/out/vo_mediacodec.c
+++ b/video/out/vo_mediacodec.c
@@ -2735,6 +2735,17 @@ static void stats_tick(struct vo *vo)
     }
 }
 
+// Under osd.lock once the workers run. A delayed plane is presented on every
+// video frame, not only when its content changes: on Amlogic, a plane a
+// refresh behind its picture that updated only with its content put a judder
+// pair into the video at most updates, and one updated on every frame put in
+// none.
+static void osd_set_vsync_delay(struct priv *p, int delay)
+{
+    p->osd_vsync_delay = delay;
+    p->osd.repeat_unchanged = delay > 0;
+}
+
 static void osd_init(struct vo *vo)
 {
     struct priv *p = vo->priv;
@@ -2822,7 +2833,7 @@ static int preinit(struct vo *vo)
     p->osd_surface = opts->osd_surface;
     if (!mediacodec_geometry_parse(opts->video_rect, &p->osd_geometry))
         MP_WARN(vo, "Invalid --vo-mediacodec-video-rect; ignoring geometry.\n");
-    p->osd_vsync_delay = opts->osd_vsync_delay;
+    osd_set_vsync_delay(p, opts->osd_vsync_delay);
     p->letterbox_fill = opts->letterbox_fill;
     m_config_cache_set_wakeup_cb(p->opts_cache, opts_wakeup, vo);
     vo->hwdec_devs = hwdec_devices_create();
@@ -3039,7 +3050,7 @@ static void update_opts(struct vo *vo)
         p->osd_surface = opts->osd_surface;
         if (geometry_ok)
             p->osd_geometry = geometry;
-        p->osd_vsync_delay = opts->osd_vsync_delay;
+        osd_set_vsync_delay(p, opts->osd_vsync_delay);
         p->letterbox_fill = opts->letterbox_fill;
         osd_init(vo);
         vo->want_redraw = true;
@@ -3047,7 +3058,7 @@ static void update_opts(struct vo *vo)
     if (!p->osd_threads_created)
         return;
     mp_mutex_lock(&p->osd.lock);
-    p->osd_vsync_delay = opts->osd_vsync_delay;
+    osd_set_vsync_delay(p, opts->osd_vsync_delay);
     bool changed = geometry_ok &&
                    !mediacodec_geometry_equal(p->osd_geometry, geometry);
     if (changed)
